Day 12 — Trees 🌳

First, remember what a tree looks like:
       1
      / \
     2   3


Node 1 is the root. Node 2 is its left child, and node 3 is its right child.
What does recursion mean here?
Recursion means a function calls itself. In tree problems, the function can call itself on the left child and right child to solve smaller parts of the tree.
Imagine we have a function called process(node):
- process(1) works on the whole tree.
- process(2) works on the subtree starting at node 2.
- process(3) works on the subtree starting at node 3.
The key idea is that each child can be treated as the root of its own smaller tree.
