Topic 1: Quick revision of tree basics
Look at this tree:
       10
      /  \
     5    15
    / \
   3   7


- Root: 10 — the top node.
- Parent: 5 is the parent of 3 and 7.
- Leaf: 3, 7, and 15 — nodes with no children.
- Depth: number of edges from the root; node 7 has depth 2.
- Height: longest path from a node down to a leaf; the root has height 2 edges, or 3 nodes along that path.
